WEBVTT

00:00:18.340 --> 00:00:19.710
“You judge a man by his looks”!

00:00:19.710 --> 00:00:21.870
Randy, you’re the one 
who always says that!

00:00:22.910 --> 00:00:24.420
Sorry to interrupt your meal!

00:00:24.660 --> 00:00:26.680
You’ve been ordered to sortie!

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:31.010
The Wulgaru army has broken 
past our absolute defense zone!

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:06.550
“Defensive Battle at
Cosmopolitan Academy (First Part)”

00:02:09.940 --> 00:02:15.370
Delish! Ashagi, ish dis 
your weal calling in life?

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:17.460
Why are you eating?

00:02:17.790 --> 00:02:19.830
The operation has already started!

00:02:19.830 --> 00:02:22.590
I’m bored stiff after 
all of this waiting.

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:26.970
Hey, Izuru! How was 
your date with Teoria?

00:02:30.890 --> 00:02:34.470
“How,” huh? Everyone saw 
how it went down, right?

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:37.690
We only got to talk for a 
bit before I was summoned.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:40.600
But-but a date is still a date!

00:02:40.600 --> 00:02:44.970
You suddenly grew closer or something 
along those lines, right?

00:02:45.230 --> 00:02:48.270
Well, I’ll admit I do 
think we’ve grown closer.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:50.160
Ange is running late!

00:02:50.160 --> 00:02:51.620
What could be keeping her?

00:02:53.990 --> 00:02:57.540
Black 6 is already in position 
to sortie and will be

00:02:57.540 --> 00:02:59.240
working independently of you.

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:03.090
We just received an emergency 
call from Captain Amane.

00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:06.460
Our vessel will change its current 
course and return to Earth.

00:03:06.920 --> 00:03:10.310
However, Black 6 will continue 
to head toward the frontlines.

00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:14.600
We’ve identified an enemy 
detachment headed for Earth.

00:03:14.600 --> 00:03:18.090
We believe they are targeting 
Gurantseere Cosmopolitan Academy.

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:21.010
Our school...?

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:42.460
The allied armies of Bela-Russia,

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:45.360
the Great Chinese Alliance and the MJP

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:47.510
are currently fighting 
the Wulgaru fleet that

00:03:47.510 --> 00:03:49.450
has broken past the 
absolute defense zone.

00:03:49.970 --> 00:03:51.830
However, we noticed a detachment

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:54.780
that is acting independently 
of the main fleet.

00:03:55.390 --> 00:03:57.930
Here is an image of the enemy 
squad headed toward Earth.

00:03:58.680 --> 00:03:59.880
It’s a small group...

00:04:00.240 --> 00:04:01.760
Doesn’t the fighter in front

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.430
look like the one Ange 
just recently thrashed?

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:06.720
Why are they going after the academy?

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.070
According to Commander Simon,

00:04:09.070 --> 00:04:13.110
they probably intend to steal 
some DNA samples from the school.

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:15.200
There are signs that the enemy stole a

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:18.200
vast amount of Earth’s 
data the other day.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:20.360
This attack is probably related 
to the information they obtained.

00:04:20.860 --> 00:04:23.990
At the moment, our vessel 
is the closest one to Earth.

00:04:24.750 --> 00:04:27.000
Earth will also launch 
their reserve fleet.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:29.620
We are to go and offer our support.

00:04:37.430 --> 00:04:40.140
Klein, what are you doing there?

00:04:40.690 --> 00:04:43.340
You have not received orders to sortie.

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:46.330
I’m not going to let 
you hog all of the glory.

00:04:46.330 --> 00:04:48.480
I’m going to take 
these lamata for myself!

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:50.110
Restrain yourself, Klein!

00:04:50.400 --> 00:04:52.420
The purpose of this operation

00:04:52.420 --> 00:04:54.770
is to verify the information 
Lumes has obtained.

00:04:55.570 --> 00:04:58.410
It is a reconnaissance mission 
to determine whether or not

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:01.200
the Earthlings possess prime DNA 
samples on their home world.

00:05:01.660 --> 00:05:04.780
Furthermore, your wounds 
have not yet healed.

00:05:05.580 --> 00:05:08.000
These injuries can’t hold me back!

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:11.040
If the genes are there, I’ll 
simply swipe them all!

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:15.550
I’m gonna restore 
the honor I’ve lost!

00:05:15.550 --> 00:05:16.500
Klein!

00:05:16.840 --> 00:05:18.670
These are my lamata!

00:05:22.980 --> 00:05:26.400
Lumes, remain where you 
are for the time being.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:29.890
No. We shall charge 
through, just as planned.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:33.430
With two squads, this will make a 
coordinated effort all the easier.

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:35.450
Going by the looks of it,

00:05:35.450 --> 00:05:37.550
Klein may very well fire 
at friend and foe alike.

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:40.150
Remain on standby for now 
and see how things progress.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:44.330
My fleet shall work to maintain 
our current standing.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:46.370
Very well, Sir.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:50.540
My plans have gone horribly awry...

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:56.400
No... Perhaps he predicted that 
there was a chance this may happen.

00:05:59.390 --> 00:06:02.140
Here is the information on Earth 
that I obtained the other day.

00:06:02.810 --> 00:06:05.850
According to this, the Earthlings 
have a facility where they

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:07.890
combine advanced genes on their

00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:11.190
home planet to produce highly 
advanced individuals.

00:06:11.880 --> 00:06:13.650
What an absurd species.

00:06:13.650 --> 00:06:18.600
Ultimately, they have created nothing 
but a poor imitation of our civilization.

00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:23.640
Yet even so, fascinating individuals 
can appear on occasion.

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:27.070
If not for that, this 
would be far too tiresome.

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:33.540
Here is the information on 
Pleguzesia Teoria and Daneel.

00:06:33.540 --> 00:06:35.580
As suspected, they are on Earth.

00:06:36.230 --> 00:06:37.880
My prediction was right.

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:41.330
Perhaps my younger sister’s 
genes were calling out to me...

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:45.170
It would seem that Pleguzesia 
is near this facility.

00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:48.140
I do not know if those 
of Earth apprehended her

00:06:48.140 --> 00:06:52.260
or if she went to Earth 
on her own accord.

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:54.390
Have you reported to my brother yet?

00:06:54.650 --> 00:06:56.190
I have not told anyone.

00:06:56.530 --> 00:06:59.060
I felt that it would be appropriate 
to report to you first.

00:06:59.490 --> 00:07:00.780
Keep it that way.

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:03.820
Henceforth, you are to be 
my eyes and ears as you

00:07:03.820 --> 00:07:05.460
continue to gather information.

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:07.170
Is it safe to assume that you

00:07:07.170 --> 00:07:08.860
do not want me to submit 
an official report?

00:07:09.160 --> 00:07:11.540
I do not want to distress 
my older brother.

00:07:12.380 --> 00:07:14.520
And if this information came to light,

00:07:14.520 --> 00:07:18.870
ambitious fools would try their 
upmost best to topple our clan.

00:07:19.310 --> 00:07:21.920
What is my younger 
sister doing on Earth?

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:24.290
Until that is made clear, 
do not tell anyone.

00:07:24.570 --> 00:07:25.630
Understood.

00:07:26.060 --> 00:07:28.780
I will speak with my brother

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:31.260
and see to it that you 
are sent to Earth.

00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:35.640
But I must take other 
measures, just in case.

00:07:36.650 --> 00:07:41.020
To think that he had foreseen 
that I may not land on Earth...

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:43.600
Pleguzes Jiart...

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:47.790
Just how far can his eyes 
see into the future?

00:07:58.670 --> 00:08:02.130
I imagine the Wulgaru fleet we’re 
currently facing on the frontlines

00:08:02.130 --> 00:08:04.300
is a diversion meant 
to draw our attention.

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:06.460
I think their real target is Earth.

00:08:06.930 --> 00:08:10.260
Isn’t this the first time they’ve 
landed a direct attack on Earth?

00:08:10.850 --> 00:08:12.600
I hope everyone evacuates in time...

00:08:12.940 --> 00:08:15.720
We just received some new 
information from Commander Simon.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:18.480
The commander of the enemy’s 
infiltration squad is Klein.

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:21.320
Supposedly he is one of the 
Wulgaru’s Military Commanders.

00:08:21.320 --> 00:08:22.570
A Military Commander?

00:08:22.570 --> 00:08:24.950
What’s that? Sounds kinda tough!

00:08:24.950 --> 00:08:27.910
Once you’ve entered combat air 
space, launch out of your cockpits.

00:08:27.910 --> 00:08:30.750
After that, our main ship will 
engage in artillery combat.

00:08:30.750 --> 00:08:32.570
Everyone, prepare to sortie.

00:08:33.170 --> 00:08:35.910
Here are the routes we expect 
the enemy to take to Earth.

00:08:36.500 --> 00:08:38.920
It’s hard to say whether we 
can catch up with them or not.

00:08:39.300 --> 00:08:42.540
In the end, they may breach 
the earth’s atmosphere.

00:08:42.540 --> 00:08:45.920
The GDF’s reserve fleet has 
reached the first line of defense.

00:08:45.920 --> 00:08:47.250
They will engage in combat.

00:08:57.980 --> 00:09:01.220
Do you think those measly 
ships are enough to stop me?

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:04.440
Speed up! We’re gonna 
send these wimps reeling!

00:09:15.710 --> 00:09:18.880
Topeka of the GDF squadron Providence 
has been severely damaged!

00:09:18.880 --> 00:09:21.050
Galveston and Little Rock 
have been destroyed.

00:09:21.710 --> 00:09:23.420
The enemy fleet hasn’t 
suffered any losses!

00:09:23.420 --> 00:09:25.500
They will enter range within 20 seconds.

00:09:25.800 --> 00:09:27.780
All ships, prepare to launch an assault.

00:09:27.780 --> 00:09:29.680
You are free to use 
all of your artillery.

00:09:29.680 --> 00:09:32.320
Commence fire once enemy 
fighters are within range.

00:09:32.320 --> 00:09:34.600
Your targets are the enemy 
squad on track for Earth!

00:09:34.600 --> 00:09:38.110
The enemy fighters seem to have 
rather advance evasion systems.

00:09:38.110 --> 00:09:39.520
I’m not sure if we’ll hit them...

00:09:39.520 --> 00:09:41.650
We don’t have to hit them.

00:09:41.650 --> 00:09:43.640
We just have to slow them down a bit.

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:48.030
I never expected our main ship 
to engage in actual combat...

00:09:48.030 --> 00:09:50.700
That goes to show how 
dire the situation is.

00:09:50.700 --> 00:09:52.860
Depending on how things 
go, we may find ourselves

00:09:52.860 --> 00:09:54.350
strapped to a gun.

00:09:54.350 --> 00:09:56.000
That isn’t funny!

00:09:56.000 --> 00:09:59.110
I always get a Rank 
C at target practice.

00:10:08.000 --> 00:10:09.080
All ships, blast off!

00:10:33.990 --> 00:10:35.280
Reinforcements?

00:10:39.410 --> 00:10:41.530
But I don’t have time 
to play with them!

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.420
You’re in the way!

00:11:13.060 --> 00:11:14.650
The enemy squad has 
suffered minor damages!

00:11:15.200 --> 00:11:16.790
The enemies are moving at high speeds,

00:11:16.790 --> 00:11:18.620
allowing them to dodge our attacks.

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:20.670
Even when we do hit them, 
it doesn’t do anything.

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:22.830
As suspected, it looks like 
they are equipped with

00:11:22.830 --> 00:11:24.620
high-performance defense systems.

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:28.920
Yeah... They’ll get away if we 
use normal shells and artillery.

00:11:29.430 --> 00:11:31.920
But that might work...

00:11:31.920 --> 00:11:33.250
Do you have an idea?

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:35.980
I modified the weapon we used at Ceres.

00:11:35.980 --> 00:11:38.180
It’s a powerful 
long-range optical weapon

00:11:38.180 --> 00:11:39.920
that pierces through objects 
at the speed of light.

00:11:40.230 --> 00:11:43.270
But I’m afraid the enemy will 
notice before we can fire a shot

00:11:43.270 --> 00:11:45.710
if we don’t snipe from 
a substantial distance.

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:54.150
Crap! At this rate, they’re 
gonna break through.

00:11:54.530 --> 00:11:57.510
But their speed has definitely dropped.

00:11:57.510 --> 00:12:00.530
If they maintain this pace, 
we should make it in time.

00:12:00.960 --> 00:12:02.540
We have to stop the Wulgaru!

00:12:02.540 --> 00:12:05.240
We can’t let them lay a single 
finger on our old school.

00:12:07.410 --> 00:12:11.750
Your assignment is to evaluate 
yourself and then surpass yourself.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:14.960
You’ve reached the 
designated airspace!

00:12:14.960 --> 00:12:17.430
Team Rabbits, prepare to sortie.

00:12:17.430 --> 00:12:20.380
But we are going to change 
Gold 4’s armament.

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:21.920
We’re changing it?

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:28.640
Team Rabbits, blast off!

00:13:52.570 --> 00:13:55.150
Go to Hell!

00:13:59.450 --> 00:14:01.400
You still haven’t seen nothin’ yet!

00:14:01.990 --> 00:14:05.150
I dare you to come at me all 
at once, you pathetic wimps!

00:14:05.150 --> 00:14:08.820
Even in mass, you’re nothing 
before the great Black 6!

00:14:09.230 --> 00:14:11.490
That’s one feisty pilot, huh?

00:14:12.050 --> 00:14:14.920
Supposedly this is Ange 
Kuroki’s fighting style.

00:14:14.920 --> 00:14:17.210
Compared to him, Patrick is...

00:14:18.470 --> 00:14:20.930
Tamaki isn’t coming, is she...?

00:14:22.220 --> 00:14:24.100
Get yer act together, Patrick!

00:14:24.100 --> 00:14:25.880
What happened to all that vigor 
you had just a minute ago?

00:14:26.100 --> 00:14:29.840
It looks like I’m the type that 
uses love as energy in my fights...

00:14:30.060 --> 00:14:32.300
Go meet your maker!

00:14:32.780 --> 00:14:35.020
Oh, Tamaki...

00:14:35.240 --> 00:14:36.890
Dang, they’re the polar opposites.

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:38.490
Black 6, huh?

00:14:38.490 --> 00:14:40.340
I hope this is the only time we have to

00:14:40.340 --> 00:14:41.980
fight alongside someone like him.

00:14:51.920 --> 00:14:53.660
They dived into inner space!

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:54.910
Let’s go after them!

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:58.220
Wait! We’re outfitted for 
fighting in outer space.

00:14:58.220 --> 00:14:59.890
If we get caught in Earth’s gravity,

00:14:59.890 --> 00:15:01.460
we’ll become shooting stars 
and get burned to a crisp!

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:03.430
Red 5 and Blue 1,

00:15:03.430 --> 00:15:05.920
use Rose 3 as a shield 
and descend to Earth.

00:15:05.920 --> 00:15:07.880
Will that actually work?

00:15:07.880 --> 00:15:11.480
Rose 3 is capable of entering the 
earth’s atmosphere in its basic form.

00:15:11.480 --> 00:15:14.230
If you cling to the back of 
Rose 3 while its shield is up,

00:15:14.230 --> 00:15:16.720
Blue 1 and Red 5 should be 
able to handle the entry.

00:15:16.720 --> 00:15:18.920
Purple 2, stay there on standby.

00:15:18.920 --> 00:15:21.450
Help direct the units and 
coordinate their formations.

00:15:21.450 --> 00:15:25.150
Roger. I will begin calculating their 
speed of descent and angle of incidence.

00:15:26.620 --> 00:15:28.240
We’re off and away!

00:15:31.630 --> 00:15:33.820
I’m sending you my 
orbital calculations.

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:38.130
Rose 3 is faster than their fighters,

00:15:38.130 --> 00:15:39.800
so you’ll just barely beat them there.

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:42.430
But if you stray from this 
course even a little,

00:15:42.430 --> 00:15:45.040
you’ll wind up at a totally 
different location. Be careful!

00:15:45.040 --> 00:15:48.210
Got it! I’m heading on out!

00:15:55.860 --> 00:15:57.560
We’re falling!

00:15:58.320 --> 00:16:00.310
My unit’s surface temperature 
is rapidly increasing!

00:16:00.820 --> 00:16:02.110
We’re still in the green!

00:16:02.110 --> 00:16:03.940
Tamaki, up the speed!

00:16:04.190 --> 00:16:06.150
Rose 3, you can do it!

00:16:31.480 --> 00:16:32.560
We made it!

00:16:41.860 --> 00:16:42.810
Whoa!

00:16:43.070 --> 00:16:44.270
Did your unit get damaged?

00:16:44.450 --> 00:16:46.370
It’s just heavier 
than I was expecting.

00:16:46.370 --> 00:16:47.420
Relax!

00:16:47.420 --> 00:16:52.500
As long as you keep your 
cool, you can handle this!

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:55.910
Got it! Keep my cool... Keep my cool...

00:17:05.670 --> 00:17:08.640
I can’t believe we’re running 
away when the enemy is right there!

00:17:08.640 --> 00:17:10.180
It can’t be helped...

00:17:10.180 --> 00:17:11.810
What’s going on up there?

00:17:12.520 --> 00:17:13.800
It’s the Fail Five!

00:17:13.800 --> 00:17:15.190
The Fail Five?

00:17:15.730 --> 00:17:19.730
Yeah! Blue 1, Rose 3 and Red 
5 are up there fighting!

00:17:19.730 --> 00:17:21.470
You mean Izuru, Asagi and Tamaki?

00:17:21.610 --> 00:17:23.400
Hang in there! Fight!

00:17:33.250 --> 00:17:34.540
One fighter down!

00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:36.420
I can see our school from here!

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:41.270
It’s going to take a while 
before Gold 4 is ready.

00:17:41.270 --> 00:17:43.170
Please buy some time!

00:17:43.170 --> 00:17:44.720
There are a bunch of enemy fighters!

00:17:44.720 --> 00:17:46.170
Tell us what to do, Kei.

00:17:46.550 --> 00:17:48.540
Klein is their primary fighter.

00:17:48.540 --> 00:17:52.100
Someone mark him while the other two 
deal with the remaining fighters.

00:17:54.850 --> 00:17:57.750
Izuru, you should defeat Klein.

00:17:57.750 --> 00:17:59.760
Tamaki and I will handle the others.

00:18:00.020 --> 00:18:01.310
Huh? But...

00:18:01.480 --> 00:18:04.030
Red 5 is superior in combat.

00:18:04.030 --> 00:18:06.270
Leave the others to us.

00:18:06.850 --> 00:18:08.980
You do your job as the ace!

00:18:09.450 --> 00:18:11.570
All right. I’m leaving 
the rest to you.

00:18:11.990 --> 00:18:14.860
Izuru was Team Rabbit’s ace pilot?!

00:18:15.250 --> 00:18:19.240
I hate to admit it, but he’s a 
better pilot than either of us.

00:18:19.590 --> 00:18:21.970
So we should focus on doing what we can.

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:26.580
Dang! And here I thought 
I was our ace pilot!

00:18:28.800 --> 00:18:29.930
Great!

00:18:30.140 --> 00:18:33.390
All three of them have high Harmonic 
Levels, especially Blue 1.

00:18:33.850 --> 00:18:35.770
This may be his highest level yet.

00:18:37.760 --> 00:18:40.090
The primitive creature 
I fought last time?

00:18:40.090 --> 00:18:41.050
Excellent!

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:42.720
Let’s have a return match!

00:18:43.030 --> 00:18:44.920
My weapons don’t work on him...

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:45.890
What should I do?

00:18:49.070 --> 00:18:50.730
Thanks for waitin’!

00:18:50.730 --> 00:18:53.070
Gold 4 is now on the scene!

00:18:53.490 --> 00:18:55.830
Izuru and the others have already 
made contact with the enemy.

00:18:55.830 --> 00:18:57.570
Please prepare to fire immediately.

00:18:57.830 --> 00:18:59.460
Don’t be in such a rush!

00:18:59.460 --> 00:19:02.040
Optical weapons take a delicate touch.

00:19:02.040 --> 00:19:03.960
They pierce through the 
enemy at the speed of light,

00:19:03.960 --> 00:19:06.660
so as long as your aim is good, there 
is zero chance of them dodging!

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:10.390
In exchange, they require 
pin-point accuracy.

00:19:10.390 --> 00:19:12.920
And there is a crazy huge distance 
between me and my target!

00:19:12.920 --> 00:19:16.210
I’ve gotta account for the earth’s 
rotation, vibrations in the atmosphere

00:19:16.210 --> 00:19:17.600
and even gravitational interference!

00:19:17.600 --> 00:19:20.420
Hey, at least I don’t have to 
worry about the Coriolis Effect

00:19:20.420 --> 00:19:22.310
like I do when sniping on Earth.

00:19:22.310 --> 00:19:25.180
To top it off, I’ve 
gotta fire at max power.

00:19:25.400 --> 00:19:28.150
So once I let her rip, it’ll take 
a while before I can fire again.

00:19:28.860 --> 00:19:30.840
Even on Earth, I’m 
probably the only person

00:19:30.840 --> 00:19:32.730
capable of pulling this mission off!

00:19:36.910 --> 00:19:39.750
We’ll help adjust the laser’s sight.

00:19:39.750 --> 00:19:41.920
But since the enemy is moving,

00:19:41.920 --> 00:19:43.750
everything ultimately rests 
on the skill of the gunner.

00:19:44.170 --> 00:19:45.090
Be careful.

00:19:45.090 --> 00:19:48.120
I know, I know! You can count on me!

00:19:49.260 --> 00:19:50.970
I want something if I pull this off.

00:19:50.970 --> 00:19:56.250
Like one of the GDF’s 
G-11, Steyr-ACE or IWS-2000!

00:19:56.250 --> 00:19:57.760
All right. I’ll take 
it into consideration.

00:19:57.760 --> 00:19:58.920
Fer real?!

00:19:59.390 --> 00:20:01.510
You may pull the trigger 
when you’re ready,

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:03.340
but don’t take too long.

00:20:03.640 --> 00:20:05.190
I know you can do it.

00:20:05.690 --> 00:20:08.520
You’re really pilin’ on the 
pressure by actin’ all nice...

00:20:10.650 --> 00:20:12.850
Gold 4 is ready to snipe.

00:20:12.850 --> 00:20:14.690
Do something to restrict 
the enemy’s movements.

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:15.770
In that case--!

00:20:43.490 --> 00:20:45.730
Now you’ve done it, 
primitive creature!

00:20:45.730 --> 00:20:48.680
How dare you make me lick 
your planet’s dirt!

00:20:48.680 --> 00:20:50.720
Hurry, while the enemy is still dazed!

00:20:52.660 --> 00:20:54.280
Don’t push me!

00:20:54.700 --> 00:20:57.480
If I’m not careful, Izuru 
might get caught in the blast!

00:23:41.060 --> 00:23:56.080
“Defensive Battle at
Cosmopolitan Academy (Second Part)”
